2. STELLAR MASS / IMF: is any IMF heavier than the JAM ceiling allowed by the galaxy's own inner kinematics?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Salpeter population mass (ATLAS3D XX, r band): law over-predicts the JAM mass inside r12 by median +0.047 dex (mean +0.058); 13/16 galaxies over-predicted
  SLUGGS mass (K-band, ~Kroupa/Chabrier-like): inner excess median +0.004 dex; 8/16 over-predicted
  canonical: outer offset with Salpeter masses +0.2164 (+6.85 sigma); with SLUGGS masses +0.2587 (+7.78 sigma)
  alt      : outer offset with Salpeter masses +0.2150 (+6.83 sigma); with SLUGGS masses +0.2570 (+7.76 sigma)
  stellar mass that nulls each outer offset, relative to the JAM-law ceiling: median +0.490 dex (range +0.10..+0.92); it would over-predict the inner JAM mass by median +0.488 dex
  -> an IMF heavier than the JAM ceiling is excluded by each galaxy's own inner kinematics under the law; an IMF gradient that is bottom-heavy only in the core (the measured sense) lowers the outer stellar mass and enlarges the deficit.

